rem Counting Fractions in a Range
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=73
rem Count reduced fractions between 1/3
rem and 1/2, denominators up to a limit

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option Limit integer = 12000

rem Moebius of 1 to Limit from the
rem primes up to the root: a repeated
rem prime gives 0, else the sign counts
rem the primes, plus one if a larger
rem prime is left over.
Root = Limit isqrt
Ps = primes to Root array
Num = 1 to Limit array
N = Num reshape 1 Limit
Col = Ps reshape (Ps len) 1
Divs = N mod Col equal 0
Twice = N mod (Col * Col) equal 0
Square = Twice any axis 0
Count = Divs count axis 0
Kept = Divs choose Col 1
Flip = Kept transpose
Core = Flip reduce * rank 1
Quo = Num // Core
Left = Quo greater 1
Extra = Left choose 1 0
Odd = (Count + Extra) mod 2
Signs = 1 - Odd * 2
Mu = Square choose 0 Signs

rem All fractions strictly between, by
rem denominator, then prefix totals. A
rem Moebius sum keeps the reduced ones.
D = 1 to Limit
Per = (D - 1) // 2 - D // 3
Tot = Per scan + with 0
Quot = Limit // D
Answer = (Mu * (Tot Quot)) sum
Answer print
